  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Doing Business In Conflict Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">What is the starting point for the project?The conflicts in Sudan and the Palestinian Terrtories have a major impact on the ability of Entrepreneur Support Organizations (ESOs) and businesses to keep running their operations in order to provide income, services and products that are needed on the ground. Many in Sudan have relocated and are restarting operations, while in Gaza and the West Bank, businesses also need to adjust and cope with the current situation.Which problem will be solved and what is the goal?Despite the immense resilience of ESOs and young entrepreneurs, disturbed infrastructure, the dire circumstances, having to flee the city or country and experiencing a great uncertainty of the future have led to even more volatile context for entrepreneurs to work in, causing the entrepreneurs and ESOs not to able to cope with the situation. This in turn results in added fragility due to the loss of income, services rendered and products delivered. As well as a loss effective of support systems and mechanisms to maintain economic activities.How does this project solve the problem? This project aims to provide support and tools to ESOs and young entrepreneurs in Sudan and the Palestinian Territories, enabling them to learn about and apply concrete business tactics and tools in running their business during the conflicts.Where?Sudan and the Palestinian Territories.</narrative>
  </description>
